'''Island Invasion Tour 2026''' is an upcoming professional wrestling pay-per-view event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], scheduled to be held on August 9, 2026 at the Fangatapu National Stadium in [[Fangatapu]], [[Vaiahi Islands]]. It will be the annual [[Island Invasion Tour]] event — NOPW's annual homecoming to the Vaiahi Islands, the homeland of [[IGO Heavyweight Championship|IGO Heavyweight Champion]] [[Leoni Masua]] — and the first major pay-per-view since the [[Shendan Cup 2026]] in June. The event is expected to feature nine matches, with five championships on the line, and will be headlined by Leoni Masua defending the IGO Heavyweight Championship against [[KAZUKI (wrestler)|KAZUKI]] in a rematch of their January 2025 and July 2025 encounters.

This will be the first Island Invasion Tour held in Fangatapu since Leoni reclaimed the IGO Heavyweight Championship at the Shendan Cup on June 12, 2026. The event is expected to draw the largest live crowd in Island Invasion history, with the Vaiahi public treating the show as a national celebration.

== Background ==

The [[Island Invasion Tour]] is NOPW's annual touring event through the Vaiahi Islands, [[Yanbaru]], and [[Nakamizu]] — the homeland of Leoni Masua and the Vaiahi diaspora. The tour is the most culturally significant event on the NOPW calendar, blending professional wrestling with Vaiahi ceremony, wayfinding symbolism, and the warrior traditions of the Tautai people. The 2026 edition is the first Island Invasion since Leoni's second championship reign began at the Shendan Cup, and the first since the [[Fono]] of [[Vaiahi]] declared a national holiday following his title victory.

The event follows seven consecutive [[NOPW Wednesday]] shows that built the storylines converging on Fangatapu:

* '''The death of Kuroshio.''' The four former members of [[Kuroshio (stable)|Kuroshio]] — Leoni, [[Ryohei Maeda]], KAZUKI, and [[Daigo Kuroki]] — brawled at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 6|Episode 6]] and officially ended the Black Tide bond. At [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 7|Episode 7]], KAZUKI defeated Kuroki, his second consecutive victory over a former Kuroshio brother after beating Maeda at Episode 6. KAZUKI has now defeated both of Leoni's former brothers. The IGO Heavyweight Championship match at Fangatapu is a pure one-on-one contest — no Maeda, no Kuroki, no Kuroshio. Just Leoni and the man who ended his 1,095-day reign.
* '''The Cannon Club betrays Marcus Vance.''' At Episode 7, the entire Cannon Club attacked [[Marcus Vance|Marcus "The Drill" Vance]] during his main-event match against [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]]. Kengo declared Vance was "never one of us." [[Jusuf Muntasir]] then appeared and joined the assault. Vance enters Island Invasion as a lone babyface Intercontinental Champion, targeted by both his former faction and the Baliscan invader. The Vance vs. Muntasir match is the most personal non-main-event match on the card.
* '''The Vaiahi family war.''' [[Taumafa Vaiahi]] retained the [[Strong Openweight Championship]] against [[Malo Vaiahi|Malo]] at Episode 7 and challenged Kengo directly. The family hierarchy — Leoni, Kengo, Taumafa — remains unresolved. At Fangatapu, Taumafa is expected to defend the Strong Openweight Championship against Kengo, with the family war finally reaching the ring.
* '''The tag team title war.''' The [[The Usos|Usos]] have retained the [[IGO Tag Team Championship]] twice by non-clean finishes. [[Diego Reyes]] and [[Haruto Kimura]] have attacked the Usos before the bell and brawled across arenas. The Island Invasion match is expected to be a no-disqualification contest.
* '''The young guns' rise.''' [[Yuto Ono]] and [[Tetsuya Yamamoto|Tetsuya "The Fox" Yamamoto]] have defeated Cannon Club junior tag champions in consecutive tag matches. Ono has been called out by World TV Champion [[Jin Tanaka|Jin "Bulldog" Tanaka]]. The young core is ascending.
* '''The Marauder's undefeated streak.''' The mysterious powerhouse is 4-0 on Wednesday nights and has not been identified. Island Invasion may be the stage where someone finally tests him — or where his identity is revealed.
* '''Leoni's conundrum.''' At Episode 7, Leoni watched the Cannon Club betray Vance and chose not to intervene. His backstage promo revealed the impossible calculation: helping Vance helps a former Cannon Club member; letting Vance burn lets Kengo win; fighting Jusuf makes an unnecessary enemy. The Tribal Chief enters Fangatapu carrying not just the namo but the weight of a shifting battlefield.

